==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-move on.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To [[continue]]; to [[proceed]]; to [[go on]].
#: {{ux|en|After spending the night resting in an abandoned church, the group decided to '''move on''' in their quest.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive}} To start [[deal with|dealing with]] something else.
#: {{ux|en|The best revenge is always to just happily '''move on''' and let karma do the rest.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Ellie Violet Bramley|title=Ted Baker’s closure was foreseeable from a fashion perspective|date=2024-08-19|url=https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/article/2024/aug/19/ted-baker-closure-fashion-perspective|passage=Part of the problem is that Ted Baker hasn’t '''moved on'''. In an era of hyper-fast fashion, where consumers can buy into new trends in the bat of an eyelid at very low cost, Ted Baker’s dedication to its staid aesthetic read like an admission of defeat long before its actual demise. |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240830101829/https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/article/2024/aug/19/ted-baker-closure-fashion-perspective}}
#* {{RQ:Atlantic|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2025/03/israel-inquiry-october-7/682041/|title=Netanyahu Doesn’t Want the Truth to Come Out|date=2025-03-14|author=Gershom Gorenberg|passage=In Israel, a state commission of inquiry is not merely a judicial instrument or a means of settling facts. It’s a ritual of national closure that allows people to put events in order and '''move on'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250329175404/https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2025/03/israel-inquiry-october-7/682041/}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive|informal}} To attempt a seduction, often in a way seen as disloyal or rude to another.
#: {{ux|en|I think Shane is going to '''move on''' my ex tonight.}}
# To physically move something or someone.
#: {{ux|en|The police '''moved''' the protestors '''on'''.}}
# {{lb|en|AAVE|transitive}} To [[assault]] or [[attack]].

